<title>EGYPT: Citibank sets its first Egypt base rate at 9.75pct.</title>
<headline>Citibank sets its first Egypt base rate at 9.75pct.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank in Egypt said on Monday it would set a base rate periodically for the Egyptian pound for the first time in the local money market.</p>
<p>&quot;Citibank has... decided to periodically quote an Egyptian pound base rate from which it will price its overdrafts,&quot; it said in a press release. &quot;Clients will be quoted the base rate plus a spread,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>&quot;With the development of the Egyptian financial markets in size and sophistication, the need for a market determined reference rate for pricing loans has arisen.&quot;</p>
<p>The rate was set on Monday at 9.75 percent, the bank said.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
